self-test-clear-untestable: algorithms without a test leave the toDoList

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 3, TPM2_IncrementalSelfTest): "The TPM will return
in toDoList a list of algorithms that are yet to be tested. [...] Only the
algorithms on the toTest list are scheduled to be tested by this command."
and "If toDoList is empty, then no additional tests are required"; TPM2_SelfTest
with fullTest = YES "will test all functions".

TestAlgorithm() clears the bit of an algorithm that has no test (KEYEDHASH,
XOR, MGF1, ECDAA, SYMCIPHER, the KDFs, ...) only in the caller's vector, not in
g_toTest. After TPM2_SelfTest(fullTest = YES), which sets g_toTest to every
implemented algorithm, these algorithms therefore stay on the toDoList forever:
no TPM2_SelfTest or TPM2_IncrementalSelfTest naming them removes them, although
the TPM has nothing left to test (after _TPM_Init they are not listed at all).
They are now cleared in both vectors (CLEAR_BOTH), as in mstpm20 and tpm-rs.

diff --git a/src/AlgorithmTests.c b/src/AlgorithmTests.c
--- a/src/AlgorithmTests.c
+++ b/src/AlgorithmTests.c
@@ -807,7 +807,7 @@ TestAlgorithm(TPM_ALG_ID alg, ALGORITHM_VECTOR* toTest)
 	    // silently CLEAR it. Decided to just clear.
 	    if(!TEST_BIT(alg, g_implementedAlgorithms))
 		{
-		    CLEAR_BIT(alg, *toTest);
+		    CLEAR_BOTH(alg);  // tpm-rs differential testing (bug fix): also g_toTest, as mstpm20
 		    continue;
 		}
 	    // Process whatever is left.
@@ -928,7 +928,7 @@ TestAlgorithm(TPM_ALG_ID alg, ALGORITHM_VECTOR* toTest)
 		    break;
 #  endif  // ALG_ECC
 		  default:
-		    CLEAR_BIT(alg, *toTest);
+		    CLEAR_BOTH(alg);  // tpm-rs differential testing (bug fix): also g_toTest, as mstpm20
 		    break;
 		}
 	    if(result != TPM_RC_SUCCESS)
